WEBVTT

00:00.330 --> 00:03.340
Leila signs up to help at a community garden.

00:03.737 --> 00:06.798
She wants to meet people and spend time outdoors.

00:07.167 --> 00:11.032
But on Saturday she is arranging a care visit for her father, misses

00:11.045 --> 00:12.703
the bus, and stays home.

00:13.112 --> 00:17.283
After another missed session, both she and the organiser wonder whether she is

00:17.295 --> 00:19.056
simply not motivated enough.

00:20.080 --> 00:23.919
Separate wanting to do something from having a workable opportunity

00:23.932 --> 00:25.029
and following through.

00:25.413 --> 00:27.198
Does Leila still want to come?

00:27.568 --> 00:30.961
Can the care visit, journey and session fit together?

00:31.330 --> 00:34.137
Does she know where to go and what to do if delayed?

00:34.520 --> 00:38.015
A motivational speech cannot change the bus timetable.

00:38.397 --> 00:42.364
Equally, transport will not create an interest she does not have.

00:43.413 --> 00:48.541
Leila might enjoy growing plants, value helping the neighbourhood, want company, and

00:48.554 --> 00:50.748
feel guilty about disappointing people.

00:51.131 --> 00:53.108
These reasons can coexist.

00:53.478 --> 00:58.031
Intrinsic motivation means doing an activity because the activity itself is

00:58.044 --> 00:59.638
enjoyable or interesting.

01:00.047 --> 01:04.371
Extrinsic motivation means doing it for a result beyond the activity.

01:04.779 --> 01:09.307
That result can matter personally; it is not always pressure or a prize.

01:10.330 --> 01:15.611
Ryan and Deci’s paper on self-determination theory in education discusses autonomy,

01:15.904 --> 01:17.779
competence and relatedness.

01:18.188 --> 01:23.086
In ordinary language, these concern feeling that an action is your choice, feeling

01:23.099 --> 01:26.135
able to make progress, and feeling connected to others.

01:26.517 --> 01:30.191
We can use those ideas to ask about Leila’s experience.

01:30.573 --> 01:33.010
They do not tell us her answer in advance.

01:34.038 --> 01:38.770
Perhaps Leila thinks a fixed weekly slot is the only acceptable contribution.

01:39.154 --> 01:42.713
Perhaps she worries that everyone else knows more about gardening.

01:43.095 --> 01:45.379
Perhaps she does not know who will greet her.

01:45.761 --> 01:50.838
An occasional commitment, a clear first task, or a named person to meet might help

01:50.851 --> 01:51.986
with different problems.

01:52.368 --> 01:56.131
She must also be free to say the activity no longer fits.

01:57.163 --> 01:59.038
The garden’s rules matter too.

01:59.435 --> 02:03.504
Saturday mornings may suit existing members while excluding people

02:03.516 --> 02:04.728
with other commitments.

02:05.136 --> 02:09.664
A rota records garden attendance, not all the care Leila gives her father.

02:10.060 --> 02:14.613
The organiser can ask what makes taking part difficult without demanding private

02:14.626 --> 02:16.565
details as proof of commitment.

02:16.973 --> 02:20.455
Both sides still need a workable agreement and enough people to

02:20.468 --> 02:21.922
run the activity safely.

02:22.955 --> 02:27.585
Once Leila chooses a feasible arrangement, she can make an if–then plan.

02:27.994 --> 02:32.025
If the care visit finishes by ten, I will take the ten-twenty bus

02:32.038 --> 02:33.504
and meet Sam at the gate.

02:33.913 --> 02:38.084
If it runs late, I will message Sam and use the next agreed date.

02:38.492 --> 02:41.158
The plan connects a situation to an action.

02:41.566 --> 02:44.525
It cannot solve having no available transport.

02:45.538 --> 02:50.270
If Leila attends a shorter session, that shows it was possible on that occasion.

02:50.680 --> 02:55.169
It does not prove the only obstacle was transport or that she now has a habit.

02:55.578 --> 02:59.672
If she still cannot come, ask what happened before increasing pressure.

03:00.080 --> 03:04.034
A different commitment, or a decision not to reserve a regular place,

03:04.315 --> 03:05.820
may suit everyone better.

03:06.830 --> 03:11.192
When you or someone else wants to act but keeps missing it, ask: What

03:11.205 --> 03:12.557
is making it hard to do?

03:12.927 --> 03:16.677
Check interest, practical opportunity and the next step.

03:17.047 --> 03:21.282
Choose one difficulty that can be addressed, agree a change, and review

03:21.295 --> 03:22.494
what actually happened.

03:22.877 --> 03:27.533
Understanding motivation includes accepting that someone may choose to decline.
